### dollar on the name of an array assignment
$fruits=(apple pear)
>>- SC1036 1:9 -- bash rejects the unquoted parenthesis, so this is reported as a parser syntax error
>>- SC1066 1:1 -- bash rejects $name=(...), so this is a parser syntax error whose message says to remove the $
>>- SC1088 1:9 -- mvdan rejects this input, so it is reported as a syntax error, not as a lint code; the error stops at the same parenthesis
>>- SC2154 1:1 -- mvdan rejects the dollar-prefixed assignment as a syntax error, and whole-script variable checks are skipped for scripts that do not parse completely
>>- SC2281 1:1 -- mvdan rejects a dollar-prefixed array assignment; the line is reported as a syntax error instead

### dollar on an indexed append of an array
$queue[1]+=(job)
>>- SC1036 1:12 -- bash rejects the unquoted parenthesis, so this is reported as a parser syntax error
>>- SC1066 1:1 -- bash rejects $name=(...), so this is a parser syntax error whose message says to remove the $
>>- SC1087 1:1 -- mvdan rejects this line (invalid function name), so no tree is built for it; the syntax error is reported instead
>>- SC1088 1:12 -- mvdan rejects this input, so it is reported as a syntax error, not as a lint code; the error stops at the same parenthesis
>>- SC2086 1:1 -- mvdan rejects a dollar-prefixed indexed array append; the line is reported as a syntax error instead
>>- SC2154 1:1 -- mvdan rejects the dollar-prefixed assignment as a syntax error, and whole-script variable checks are skipped for scripts that do not parse completely
>>- SC2211 1:1 -- mvdan rejects a dollar-prefixed indexed array append; the line is reported as a syntax error instead
>>- SC2276 1:1 -- mvdan rejects a dollar-prefixed indexed array append; the line is reported as a syntax error instead

### dollar on a scalar assignment is left to later analysis
$fruits=apple
>>> SC2154 1:1
>>> SC2281 1:1

### no dollar but a space before the equals sign
fruits =(apple pear)
>>- SC1036 1:9 -- bash rejects the unquoted parenthesis; the parser reports =( as a syntax error
>>- SC1088 1:9 -- mvdan rejects this input, so it is reported as a syntax error, not as a lint code; the error stops at the same parenthesis
>>- SC2283 1:8 -- mvdan rejects =( after a command word as a syntax error, so the line is not linted
